nodes.statement:
Throughout this paper, we assume that~
\begin{equation} K\text{ is fixed and such that }1\leq K <\min(n,r)\text{ where }r=\mathrm{rank}(X).
\end{equation}

An active set~$(i_1,\ldots,i_K)\in\mathcal{A}_K$ is said to satisfy the {\it Irrepresentable Check} condition if 
\begin{equation} \tag{${\mathcal{A}}_{\mathrm{Irr.}}$}
\forall k\in[K],\ \forall j\notin { T^{k}}:=\{j_1,\ldots, j_k\},\quad X_j^\top X_{T^{k}}\big( X_{T^{k}}^\top  X_{T^{k}}\big)^{-1} s_{k}<1,
\end{equation}
where~$j_k$ and~$s_k$ are defined from~$i_k$ using~\eqref{e:findices}.
By a slight abuse of notation we will  denote by~\eqref{hyp:IrrAlongThePath}  the set of sequences~$(i_1,\ldots,i_K)$ that satisfy this property.

The design matrix~$X$ satisfies the Irrepresentable Condition of order~$K$ if and only if 
\begin{equation} \tag{${\mathrm{Irrep.}}$}
\forall S\subset[p]\ \text{s.t.}\ \# S\leq K,\quad
\max_{j\in[p]\setminus S}\max_{||v||_\infty\leq1} X_j^\top X_S\big(X_S^\top X_S\big)^{-1}v<1,
\end{equation}
where~$X_j$ denotes the~$j^{\text{th}}$ column of~$X$ and~$X_S$ the sub-matrix of~$X$ obtained by keeping the columns indexed by~$S$.

